TITLE:: HPtransformerRT
SUMMARY:: Classic Musical RT 8D adaptive vector transformer for real-time learning and generation
CATEGORIES:: Libraries>HPTransformer, Machine Learning
RELATED:: Classes/HPTransformerStudio

DESCRIPTION::
HPtransformerRT V30.3.0 Classic Musical RT is designed for interactive music and low-latency operation. Its main processing path uses the cleaned vector directly, without Advanced RT normalization, multiresolution history, or stability snapshots.

The default structural profile uses 8 inputs, 8 outputs, a fast window of 8, a long-term memory size of 16, a hidden size of 32, 4 attention heads of size 8, and 4 experts.

The conventional mechanisms remain available: multi-head attention, mixture of experts, long-term memory, trajectory memory, replay, surprise, protection, AutoTune, MetaLearn, and RCU. Classic profiles disable AutoTune, MetaLearn, and RCU to reduce processing load and preserve direct musical behavior.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an HPtransformerRT engine.

ARGUMENT:: inputSize
The number of input dimensions. The default value is 8.

ARGUMENT:: outputSize
The number of output dimensions. The default value is 8. outputSize must be less than or equal to inputSize.

ARGUMENT:: windowSize
The maximum size of the fast-attention context. The default value is 8.

ARGUMENT:: longMemorySize
The capacity of long-term memory and replay. The default value is 16.

ARGUMENT:: hiddenSize
The hidden dimension. The default value is 32.

ARGUMENT:: numHeads
The number of attention heads. The default value is 4.

ARGUMENT:: headSize
The dimension of each attention head. The default value is 8.

ARGUMENT:: numExperts
The number of experts. The default value is 4.

RETURNS::
An HPtransformerRT instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: learnEvent
Learns an incoming event. The engine builds a temporal pair from the previous and current events, then updates the model and any active conventional mechanisms.

ARGUMENT:: event
The current vector. With the default profile, the vector must contain 8 values.

RETURNS::
The training loss.

METHOD:: predict
Computes an output without learning.

ARGUMENT:: input
The input vector.

ARGUMENT:: requestedWindowSize
An optional fast-window size.

ARGUMENT:: requestedVelocity
An optional velocity context.

RETURNS::
A vector containing outputSize values.

METHOD:: generateStep
Generates one step from an input vector. The result is the raw engine output. The Studio's direct tracking is not applied here.

ARGUMENT:: input
The starting vector.

RETURNS::
A generated vector.

METHOD:: generate
Generates an autoregressive sequence.

ARGUMENT:: seed
The initial vector.

ARGUMENT:: count
The number of steps.

RETURNS::
An array of vectors.

METHOD:: setClassicMusicalDirect
Applies a lightweight musical profile with moderate learning, low replay, one memory recall, one trajectory recall, a generation window of 4, a slightly increased temperature, and RCU disabled.

RETURNS::
The runtime configuration.

METHOD:: setClassicUltraCPUFastLearn
Applies the minimum-CPU profile with strong adaptation for each learned event: no replay, no memory or trajectory recall, a generation window of 2, learning and generation enabled, and RCU disabled.

RETURNS::
The runtime configuration.

METHOD:: setClassicGenerationOnly
Applies a generation-only profile with external learning disabled, no replay, generation enabled, and RCU disabled.

RETURNS::
The runtime configuration.

METHOD:: setParameter
Changes a runtime parameter and propagates it to active runtimes where applicable.

ARGUMENT:: name
The parameter Symbol.

ARGUMENT:: value
The new value.

ARGUMENT:: post
Posts the change when true.

RETURNS::
The effective value.

METHOD:: setParameters
Applies a Dictionary or Event of runtime parameters.

ARGUMENT:: settings
The settings Dictionary.

ARGUMENT:: post
Posts the changes when true.

RETURNS::
The runtime configuration.

METHOD:: statusSilent
Returns a complete diagnostic without writing to the Post window.

RETURNS::
An Event.

METHOD:: enableUnifiedRCU
Enables the dual RCU runtime. Classic profiles disable it by default to reduce CPU usage.

RETURNS::
The engine.

METHOD:: disableUnifiedRCU
Disables the dual RCU runtime.

RETURNS::
The engine.

SECTION:: Default 8 x 8 configuration

CODE::
(
~hpTR = HPtransformerRT.new;
~hpTR.config.postln;
)
::

SECTION:: Equivalent explicit configuration

CODE::
~hpTR = HPtransformerRT.new(
    inputSize: 8,
    outputSize: 8,
    windowSize: 8,
    longMemorySize: 16,
    hiddenSize: 32,
    numHeads: 4,
    headSize: 8,
    numExperts: 4
);
::

SECTION:: Classic Musical Direct profile

CODE::
(
~hpTR = HPtransformerRT.new;
~hpTR.setClassicMusicalDirect;
)
::

SECTION:: Classic Ultra CPU profile

CODE::
(
~hpTR = HPtransformerRT.new;
~hpTR.setClassicUltraCPUFastLearn;
)
::

SECTION:: 8D learning and generation

CODE::
~input = [0.20,0.40,0.70,0.50,0.30,0.80,0.60,0.10];
~hpTR.learnEvent(~input);
~output = ~hpTR.generateStep(~input);
::

SECTION:: Decimation without the Studio

The setClassicUltraCPUFastLearn method configures the engine, but Learn/N decimation is handled by the Studio or the host program.

CODE::
(
~counter = 0;
~process = { |input|
    ~counter = ~counter + 1;
    if((~counter % 4) == 0, {
        ~hpTR.learnEvent(input);
    });
    ~hpTR.generateStep(input);
};
)
::

SECTION:: Direct tracking with direct method calls

Direct tracking is not built into generateStep. To reproduce the Studio's tracking behavior, apply the mix after generation.

CODE::
~mix = [0.10,0.05,0.02,0.10,0.05,0.02,0.10,0.05];
~raw = ~hpTR.generateStep(~input);
~followed = Array.fill(~raw.size, { |i|
    var amount = ~mix.wrapAt(i).clip(0.0, 1.0);
    ((~raw[i] * (1.0 - amount)) + (~input[i] * amount)).clip(0.0, 1.0);
});
::

NOTE::
Legacy normalization, multiresolution, and stability-guard parameters may still exist for archive compatibility, but the Classic Musical RT path bypasses them. They should not be used to configure this branch.
::
